groovebox-scene 1
# kick.wav and pad.wav, a long stereo file to preview.
file samples/kick.wav ours 55 0.3 1
file samples/pad.wav ours 220 10 2
# The operation count plays this scene: the most a render batch has to do. 32 voices of a stereo
# sample sound at Transpose +48 cost more than 32 of a stereo Supersaw, as measured when sample
# sounds came. Every effect slot of the four tracks holds a reverb, ringing in the busiest batch
# with every pre-delay crossfading. There a reverb in every slot costs 11,576,143 operations. With
# Pitch amount +48 and Pitch decay 10 s on top it cost 12,087,867, and a delay in every slot
# 11,250,439, each measured in a version of this scene that this file does not contain, the delay
# one with a TEMPO turn at the chord, before a sound's values were found faster and the reverb
# version cost 12,096,989. pad on pad 1 through the panel, in the place of the factory
# project's Kick: MENU + step 3, then OK opens the sound picker on Kick, and up twice onto New
# sample and OK open the sample picker on kick.wav, and down onto pad.wav and OK choose it. A tap of
# PADS/KEYS then makes the pads keys that play pad.
input 3200 press menu
input 4800 press step-3
input 6400 release step-3
input 8000 release menu
input 9600 press ok
input 11200 release ok
input 12800 press up
input 13600 release up
input 14400 press up
input 15200 release up
input 16000 press ok
input 17600 release ok
input 19200 press down
input 20800 release down
input 22400 press ok
input 24000 release ok
input 25600 press pads-keys
input 27200 release pads-keys
# Filter page: Resonance 100%.
input 28800 press page
input 30400 press step-3
input 32000 release step-3
input 33600 release page
input 35200 turn encoder-3 127
input 36800 turn encoder-3 1
# Volume envelope page: Release 10 s.
input 38400 press page
input 40000 press step-5
input 41600 release step-5
input 43200 release page
input 44800 turn encoder-4 127
# Voice page: Trigger Gate, so a note of pad plays its Release once let go. Then the Pitch page,
# whose first item is Transpose, and + held for 48 moves: +48, so the notes below read pad.wav 4 to
# 24 times as fast as it was recorded.
input 46400 press page
input 48000 press step-6
input 49600 release step-6
input 51200 release page
input 52000 turn encoder-4 -1
input 52800 press page
input 54400 press step-7
input 56000 release step-7
input 57600 release page
input 68800 press plus
input 201800 release plus
# Taps of steps 1 to 16 put a note of pad on every sixteenth of bar 1, at C4 in KEYS mode before
# any key. A tap of TEMPO turns the metronome on, which clicks on each beat while the pattern
# plays.
